From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:11:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mesa: treat RGB9_E5 as the floating-point read type it is

glReadPixels with GL_UNSIGNED_INT_5_9_9_9_REV packs floating-point
values, exactly like GL_UNSIGNED_INT_10F_11F_11F_REV, but only the
latter was exempt from the clamp that packing to a fixed-point type
needs. Reading an RGB9_E5 buffer back through its own type therefore
clamped every component to [0,1]: a texel holding 8064.0 came back as
1.0, so a glCopyImageSubData round trip through the format looked like
the copy had rewritten the source image.

Name the type in both lists. The CPU packing path stops clamping a
float read, and the blit packing path starts clamping one when
GL_CLAMP_READ_COLOR asks it to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mesa/main/readpix.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/readpix.c b/src/mesa/main/readpix.c
index 8aa55aa369194732b9ee4fd98b3b9a456ad1eb1c..582969a68ec59d0ec3a2e49998446ea75915706a 100644
--- a/src/mesa/main/readpix.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/readpix.c
@@ -121,7 +121,8 @@ _mesa_get_readpixels_transfer_ops(const struct gl_context *ctx,
       if (_mesa_get_clamp_read_color(ctx, ctx->ReadBuffer) &&
           !gles_snorm &&
           (type == GL_FLOAT || type == GL_HALF_FLOAT ||
-           type == GL_UNSIGNED_INT_10F_11F_11F_REV)) {
+           type == GL_UNSIGNED_INT_10F_11F_11F_REV ||
+           type == GL_UNSIGNED_INT_5_9_9_9_REV)) {
          transferOps |= IMAGE_CLAMP_BIT;
       }
    }
@@ -131,7 +132,8 @@ _mesa_get_readpixels_transfer_ops(const struct gl_context *ctx,
        */
       if ((_mesa_get_clamp_read_color(ctx, ctx->ReadBuffer) ||
            (type != GL_FLOAT && type != GL_HALF_FLOAT &&
-            type != GL_UNSIGNED_INT_10F_11F_11F_REV)) && !gles_snorm) {
+            type != GL_UNSIGNED_INT_10F_11F_11F_REV &&
+            type != GL_UNSIGNED_INT_5_9_9_9_REV)) && !gles_snorm) {
          transferOps |= IMAGE_CLAMP_BIT;
       }
 
